    "proof": "Apply the simultaneous Dirichlet pigeonhole argument to the Q^m+1 points k(log q_1/(2*pi),...,log q_m/(2*pi)) modulo one, partitioned into Q^m cubes of side 1/Q. The difference n of two points in one cube has every phase distance at most 1/Q. Since |1-exp(-2*pi*i*x)|^2=4*sin^2(pi*x)<=4*pi^2||x||^2, the stated energy bound follows. The witnesses cannot remain bounded as Q grows: otherwise a fixed positive n would have zero energy, forcing log(q_a)/log(q_b) rational for two multiplicatively independent members. Finally n<=Q^m implies Q^(-2)<=n^(-2/m).",
